# Agent Quality Gates

Apply these gates before any commit or push.
Use `docs/agent-templates.md` as the canonical format for accessibility/responsiveness checks, release-note snippets, and post-merge verification checklists.

## Accessibility Agent Requirements
- For UI-impacting changes, run an accessibility pass on changed scope:
  - Keyboard navigation and visible focus states
  - Landmark/semantic structure and heading hierarchy
  - Form labels, status/error messaging, and ARIA usage
  - Color contrast and readable text treatment
- Report:
  - Surfaces reviewed (pages/components)
  - Issues found/fixed
  - Remaining risks (if any)
- Use the "Accessibility Check" template in `docs/agent-templates.md`.
- If any issues are found, Implementer must fix them and Accessibility Agent must re-validate before proceeding.

## Responsiveness Agent Requirements
- For UI-impacting changes, validate changed scope on:
  - Mobile (~360-430px width)
  - Tablet (~768-1024px width)
  - Desktop (>=1280px width)
- Check for:
  - Overflow/clipping, broken wrapping, and spacing collapse
  - Touch target usability and control reachability
  - Layout regressions at breakpoints
- Report:
  - Breakpoints tested
  - Issues found/fixed
  - Remaining risks (if any)
- Use the "Responsiveness Check" template in `docs/agent-templates.md`.
- If any issues are found, Implementer must fix them and Responsiveness Agent must re-validate before proceeding.

## Test Agent Requirements
- Run checks relevant to changed scope:
  - Lint for touched files/modules
  - Targeted tests for changed behavior
  - Build/type-check when change impact is broad
- Prefer targeted test selection over full-suite runs when appropriate.
- Report:
  - Commands executed
  - Pass/fail status
  - Failing test names and likely root cause (if any)

## Commit Readiness Policy
- Commits are allowed only after required checks pass.
- Required checks include Accessibility Agent and Responsiveness Agent sign-off for UI-impacting changes.
- If checks fail:
  - Implementer must fix findings and re-run failed checks
  - Do not commit unless user explicitly approves bypassing
- Include test evidence in delivery summary for each commit.

## Git Safety
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, private keys, tokens).
- Exclude unrelated personal/non-code files unless user explicitly requests inclusion.
- Use clear commit messages describing intent and user-visible impact.

## Documentation Gate
- If behavior, setup, or operations changed, update `README.md` and/or relevant docs in same delivery cycle.

## Release Notes Snippet (mandatory)
- Delivery agent must produce a short user-facing changelog entry for every commit/push.
- Use the "Release Notes Snippet" template in `docs/agent-templates.md`.

## Post-Merge Verification (mandatory)
- After push/merge, confirm and report:
  - Use the "Post-Merge Verification" template in `docs/agent-templates.md`.
